            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="GRE12" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Greenhill</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1766">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1850"/>
                    <occupation>Secretary to the Stationary Company</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This seems possible - Godwin is in the depths of financial crisis, while
                            working on the History of the Commonwealth. He may well have sought
                            financial support from the Stationary Company. It is true, only one
                            entry is G Greenhill, but Godwin rarely uses initials unless there are
                            possibilities of confusion - and the G appears early in the contact -
                            and, given Godwin's practice of writing up the Diary from lists made, he
                            may have mistaken his first contact. The only previous contact iare 5
                            January 1814, when he write; and 21 August 1824 when he 'seeks' - and
                            probably did not find. So the G Greenhill on 18 March 1825 may have been
                            registering the first successful contact.</p>
                    </note>
